% lps-converted-from: underground.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program underground.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 8.

the events are:
    *a thing* emergenies occurs; known as emergency_occurs.
    *a thing* impropers use; known as improper_use.
    arrive station.

the actions are:
    press alarm.
    alert driver.
    stop train.
    continue to next station.
    *a thing* fines *a second thing*; known as fine.

the fluents are:
    the emergency is *a thing*; known as emergency.
    alerted.
    in station.
    stopped.
    the penalty is *a thing*; known as penalty.

the knowledge base underground includes:

initially in station.

when a thing emergenies occurs
then the emergency is the thing.

when press alarm
then alerted.

when stop train
then stopped.

when arrive station
then in station.

when continue to next station
then it is not the case that in station.

if the emergency is a thing
then press alarm.

when press alarm
then alerted.

if alerted
    and in station
then stop train.

if alerted
    and it is not the case that in station
then continue to next station.

it must not be true that
    press alarm
    and it is not the case that the emergency is a thing.


scenario one is:
    fire emergenies occurs from 2 to 3.
